[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191120] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191121] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191117] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191118] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191119] {:db/id 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" "question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193178 :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/id #uuid "e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/math-academy-id "q-161587" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=1-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=1-x\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/id #uuid "384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" "answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" "answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" "answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/id #uuid "13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/id #uuid "84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/id #uuid "00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/id #uuid "116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\ge 1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/id #uuid "2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\le 1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193205 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b0c3e30fcb7e748a80cdf98892291599967151343efe671aca790b2528039c4c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186191116 :answer-field/correct "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" "answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" "answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" "answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/id #uuid "02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/id #uuid "7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/id #uuid "2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/id #uuid "4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/id #uuid "e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378836 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2+x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/ac2b2f009daf16725be7d3a00743a1d1b75b437b936026fa2be898d94c8c93b4.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2+x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/id #uuid "3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/math-academy-id "q-161586" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" "answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" "answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" "answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/id #uuid "e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/id #uuid "ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/id #uuid "8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/id #uuid "fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/id #uuid "f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281303 :question/problem "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186379973 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/40/4073e99607c1e824f67b24bc93955b39c5b320901cd391ff3adb51444d1e1416.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/79/79e005cc03bb625657c652324db58db653882c640e94ea4b21a386676745bd14.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186407107 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0\\le y<2\\}\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71851a12f638da9604450cae0d50ed15187e850368890845d60b16b89e728bcf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/abdd434da59bb3a1bdc0ee7de398d7ea4aeae2f617f54b5a26a5bad871ba0ac4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193324 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281306 :question/problem "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186193178 :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186193178 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,\\}.\n$$"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/id #uuid "e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/math-academy-id "q-161587"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=1-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=1-x\\,\\}.\n$$"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/id #uuid "384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac"] ["answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/id #uuid "13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a"] ["answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/value "y<1-x"] ["answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/id #uuid "84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d"] ["answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/value "y=1-x"] ["answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/id #uuid "00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c"] ["answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/value "y>1-x"] ["answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/id #uuid "116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9"] ["answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/value "y\\ge 1-x"] ["answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/id #uuid "2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3"] ["answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/value "y\\le 1-x"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/correct "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/choices "answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/choices "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/choices "answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/choices "answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9"] ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/choices "answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3"] ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac"] [17592186192802 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80"] [17592186193205 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186193205 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b0c3e30fcb7e748a80cdf98892291599967151343efe671aca790b2528039c4c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4\\,\\}.\n$$"] [17592186193205 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/id #uuid "02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884"] ["answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4"] ["answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/id #uuid "7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742"] ["answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4"] ["answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/id #uuid "2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246"] ["answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4"] ["answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/id #uuid "4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80"] ["answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4"] ["answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/id #uuid "e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b"] ["answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/correct "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices "answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices "answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices "answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices "answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b"] [17592186378836 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2+x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186378836 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/ac2b2f009daf16725be7d3a00743a1d1b75b437b936026fa2be898d94c8c93b4.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2+x\\,\\}.\n$$"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/id #uuid "3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/math-academy-id "q-161586"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\,\\}.\n$$"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8"] ["answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/id #uuid "e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f"] ["answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1"] ["answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/id #uuid "ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f"] ["answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1"] ["answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/id #uuid "8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3"] ["answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1"] ["answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/id #uuid "fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649"] ["answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1"] ["answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/id #uuid "f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7"] ["answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/correct "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649"] ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7"] ["question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8"] [17592186192802 :knowledge-point/questions "question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144"] [17592186281303 :question/problem "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186379973 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186379973 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/40/4073e99607c1e824f67b24bc93955b39c5b320901cd391ff3adb51444d1e1416.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/79/79e005cc03bb625657c652324db58db653882c640e94ea4b21a386676745bd14.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$"] [17592186407107 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0\\le y<2\\}\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186407107 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71851a12f638da9604450cae0d50ed15187e850368890845d60b16b89e728bcf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/abdd434da59bb3a1bdc0ee7de398d7ea4aeae2f617f54b5a26a5bad871ba0ac4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$"] [17592186193324 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186281306 :question/problem "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"]] "retractions" [[17592186193178 :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186193178 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,}.\n$$"] [17592186193205 :question/problem "Consider the set $A$, defined by\n$A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: 4x^{2} + y^{2} > 4}$.\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n$∂A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: A A A A A}$.\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191120] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191121] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191117] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191118] [17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191119] [17592186378836 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2+x}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186378836 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/ac2b2f009daf16725be7d3a00743a1d1b75b437b936026fa2be898d94c8c93b4.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2+x\\,}.\n$$"] [17592186281303 :question/problem "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186379973 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186379973 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/40/4073e99607c1e824f67b24bc93955b39c5b320901cd391ff3adb51444d1e1416.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/79/79e005cc03bb625657c652324db58db653882c640e94ea4b21a386676745bd14.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x}.\n$$"] [17592186407107 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0\\le y<2}\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<2\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186407107 :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71851a12f638da9604450cae0d50ed15187e850368890845d60b16b89e728bcf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/abdd434da59bb3a1bdc0ee7de398d7ea4aeae2f617f54b5a26a5bad871ba0ac4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2\\,}.\n$$"] [17592186193324 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"]